 13194139533914 true] [17592186265452 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+4}{5} & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =5-4 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the solutions to $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1$ correspond to the values of $x$ at which $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ attains its maximum value.\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $0$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.$ \n\nThis solution is a quadrantal angle. To find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the cosine function. We know that the cosine function has its maximum values at\n\n$$\nx=2n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSince the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one maximum value in this period, we conclude that $x=0$ is the only solution." 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265454 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265455 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265456 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265457 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265458 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1041 "selection" 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265456 13194139533914 true] [17592186265453 1110 #uuid "b62952e8-cf53-52cf-afce-e56797d09219" 13194139533914 true] [17592186265454 1034 "x=0,\\,\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" 13194139533914 true] [17592186265454 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533914 true] [17592186265454 1111 #uuid "e1d64d19-11a7-57fe-aa72-e44a8bbdbf9a" 13194139533914 true] [17592186265455 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}" 13194139533914 true] [17592186265455 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533914 true] [17592186265455 1111 #uuid "e7076f62-2b3c-5fd5-875d-2ca2b064c12e" 1